Hi Ruchi,

Thank you for your clarification.

I would like to respectfully clarify my understanding of the points 
mentioned in your email, so that we can ensure there is no further 
misunderstanding regarding our conversation.

Regarding the reference to two offers, I would like to clarify once 
again that I did not have*two confirmed offers in hand*. What I shared 
with you were*two possible options for my future plans*, one was to 
explore my personal business plan, and the other was to explore a 
potential employment opportunity.

My understanding of the discussion was that, when you informed me that 
the*company was proceeding with a 30-day separation/notice period*, I 
was given some time to evaluate and provide my conclusion. I mentioned 
that I would be able to provide clarity regarding my future plans within 
a day or two.

I also explained that, if I found an opportunity that required me to 
join earlier, I could request early relieving, subject to the company's 
approval and completion of the required handover. Depending on the 
situation, this could potentially be within a few days, such as 1–2 or 
2–3 days, if feasible from both sides.

Regarding the statement that there was no misunderstanding regarding the 
discussion, I understand that we may have different recollections of the 
conversation. My intention in clarifying these points is simply to 
ensure that the details and context are properly documented and aligned. 
Since the discussion involves important matters related to separation, 
notice period, and my employment terms, I would appreciate having the 
key points and applicable terms confirmed over email as well.

Regarding your statement that I had already been prepared for the 
possibility of such a notice, I would like to clarify that my comment 
was based on *my awareness of the ongoing workforce reduction* and the 
uncertainty surrounding employment within the organization. In such 
circumstances, I believe it is natural for an employee to consider and 
prepare for different possibilities in order to secure their future. 
This should not necessarily be interpreted as a prior decision to leave 
the organization or as having confirmed employment elsewhere.

Regarding the employment documents, I appreciate your offer to provide 
access to them through HR. If possible, I would be grateful if the 
relevant documents could also be shared with me over email. This would 
allow me to review and cross-check the applicable terms, particularly 
regarding the notice period, and ensure that my understanding is 
consistent with the official employment documents.

I would especially appreciate confirmation of the applicable notice 
period, as I currently understand there may be different terms reflected 
in different documents:

1. The appointment letter, as I understand it, mentions a 45-day notice 
period.
2. I recall signing a document/agreement during my last appraisal that 
mentioned a 90-day notice period.
3. During our recent discussion, I understood that the company was 
proceeding with a 30-day separation/notice period.

*Could you please confirm which terms are applicable in my case and 
share the relevant document for my reference?*

I appreciate your support and would like to ensure that the transition 
is handled professionally and smoothly. I will continue to cooperate 
with the required handover and transition activities once the applicable 
terms and last working date are confirmed.

Thank you for your understanding.

Regards,
Rahul

