      days, such as 1–2 or 2–3 days, if feasible from both sides.<br>
      <br>
      Regarding the statement that there was no misunderstanding
      regarding the discussion, I understand that we may have different
      recollections of the conversation. My intention in clarifying
      these points is simply to ensure that the details and context are
      properly documented and aligned. Since the discussion involves
      important matters related to separation, notice period, and my
      employment terms, I would appreciate having the key points and
      applicable terms confirmed over email as well.<br>
      <br>
      Regarding your statement that I had already been prepared for the
      possibility of such a notice, I would like to clarify that my
      comment was based on <b>my awareness of the ongoing workforce
        reduction</b> and the uncertainty surrounding employment within
      the organization. In such circumstances, I believe it is natural
      for an employee to consider and prepare for different
      possibilities in order to secure their future. This should not
      necessarily be interpreted as a prior decision to leave the
      organization or as having confirmed employment elsewhere.<br>
      <br>
      Regarding the employment documents, I appreciate your offer to
      provide access to them through HR. If possible, I would be
